  "body": "## Why\n\nThe dashboard has repeatedly shipped defects that **every automated check was blind to**, because nothing verified that the three assets agree:\n\n- A control built its `<input>`, wrote every edit into it, and **never appended it to the DOM**. Saving was impossible for four releases, and a user found it, not CI.\n- A settings section was registered with 18 fields, served correctly by the API, and claimed by no view — so it **rendered nowhere**.\n- Six classes were emitted with no CSS rule after a bad conflict resolution dropped a stylesheet block. The page loaded, every test passed.\n- Spacing tokens were used that were **never defined**, so those declarations were dropped and elements shipped with `padding: 0` for five versions.\n\nNo Node, no jsdom, no new dependency — pure Python parsing the shipped assets.\n\n## The five guards\n\n| Guard | Measured |\n| --- | --- |\n| every `byId()` / `getElementById()` id exists in `index.html` | 149 lookups, **all resolve** |\n| every class `admin.js` applies has a rule in `admin.css` | 233 emitted, 376 rules |\n| every fallback-free `var(--token)` is defined | 48 refs, 50 tokens, **none undefined** |\n| every `VIEW_GROUPS` id has a `data-view` section | both directions |\n| every `data-view` section has a `VIEW_GROUPS` id | |\n\nEach parses the shipped asset rather than a Python mirror — **a mirror agrees with itself while the page stays blank**.\n\n## The class scan had to be built carefully\n\nA naive quoted-string capture stops at the first quote inside a template interpolation, and a nested template literal leaves an unterminated `${`. Both emit fragments that were never class names — and a noisy guard is one somebody deletes in six months.\n\nThis splits template literals on brace-depth-matched interpolations and drops words glued to an interpolation boundary. Without that filter the scan reported **five false positives** (`cc-diff-`, `claude-origin-`, `claude-state-`, `key-health-`, `req-status-`), every one a prefix concatenated with `${var}`. With it: **zero false positives** across all three assets.\n\n## Three genuine defects found\n\nRecorded rather than silently patched, each with the measurement that says which fix it wants:\n\n- **`cc-section` — a missing rule.** Its children `.cc-section-title` and `.cc-section-count` are styled while the parent is not.\n- **`cc-row-body` and `cc-rule-add` — dead class names.** Zero references anywhere: no CSS, no selector, no test. Deleting them from `admin.js` is the fix, not styling them.\n\nClosing any of these by guessing at spacing risks a visual regression these guards cannot see, and this is a test-only change — so they are allow-listed with reasons rather than patched here.\n\n## Verification\n\n**Full suite: 6 failed, 4359 passed, 26 skipped** vs baseline `6 failed, 4350 passed` — same six PowerShell installer failures, +9 for the new tests, zero regressions. ruff format, ruff check, ty: clean.\n\n**Every guard mutation-tested, each confirmed to fail by name**, then restored:\n\n| Mutation | Failed |\n| --- | --- |\n| renamed `id=\"sectionNav\"` | id-lookup guard |\n| renamed the `.onboarding-highlight` rule | class guard |\n| renamed the `--line-strong` definition | token guard |\n| renamed `data-view=\"providers\"` | both view guards |\n\n`admin_static/` confirmed clean afterwards.\n\n## No version bump\n\n`tests/` is explicitly not a production path in this project's versioning rules, and nothing outside `tests/contracts/` is touched.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The three allow-listed classes remain unstyled. They are cosmetic and inert, but the guard is blind to them until someone acts on the entries.\n- The class scan deliberately skips `classList.add(...)` arguments that are not bare string literals. That is a coverage gap chosen over noise, and it is stated in the code.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
